.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/locate-path Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "locate-path [![Build Status](https://travis-ci.com/sindresorhus/locate-path.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.com/github/sindresorhus/locate-path)"
.PP
.RS 4
Get the first path that exists on disk of multiple paths 
.RE
.PP
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install locate\-path
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
Here we find the first file that exists on disk, in array order\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const locatePath = require('locate\-path');

const files = [
    'unicorn\&.png',
    'rainbow\&.png', // Only this one actually exists on disk
    'pony\&.png'
];

(async () => {
    console(await locatePath(files));
    //=> 'rainbow'
})();
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "locatePath(paths, options?)"
Returns a \fRPromise<string>\fP for the first path that exists or \fRundefined\fP if none exists\&.
.SS "paths"
Type: \fRIterable<string>\fP

.PP
Paths to check\&.
.SS "options"
Type: \fRobject\fP
.SS "concurrency"
Type: \fRnumber\fP\\ Default: \fRInfinity\fP\\ Minimum: \fR1\fP

.PP
Number of concurrently pending promises\&.
.SS "preserveOrder"
Type: \fRboolean\fP\\ Default: \fRtrue\fP

.PP
Preserve \fRpaths\fP order when searching\&.

.PP
Disable this to improve performance if you don't care about the order\&.
.SS "cwd"
Type: \fRstring\fP\\ Default: \fRprocess\&.cwd()\fP

.PP
Current working directory\&.
.SS "type"
Type: \fRstring\fP\\ Default: \fR'file'\fP\\ Values: \fR'file' | 'directory'\fP

.PP
The type of paths that can match\&.
.SS "allowSymlinks"
Type: \fRboolean\fP\\ Default: \fRtrue\fP

.PP
Allow symbolic links to match if they point to the chosen path type\&.
.SS "locatePath\&.sync(paths, options?)"
Returns the first path that exists or \fRundefined\fP if none exists\&.
.SS "paths"
Type: \fRIterable<string>\fP

.PP
Paths to check\&.
.SS "options"
Type: \fRobject\fP
.SS "cwd"
Same as above\&.
.SS "type"
Same as above\&.
.SS "allowSymlinks"
Same as above\&.
